    "source": "eQUEST/DOE-2.2-47h2 SIM output; source file: house_of_worship_proposed.SIM; weather file: CHICAGO OHARE INT IL.",
    "disclaimer": "The eQUEST SIM report identifies January through December but does not establish an explicit simulation calendar year. A nominal non-leap reference year (2001) is used only to encode BPOR monthly interval timestamps; it is not an assertion that the simulation represents 2001.",
    "notes": "PS-E monthly electric end-use values are serialized directly in their native kWh. PS-F monthly natural-gas values are reported in therms and converted to kWh using the DOE-2 LV-M conversion convention printed in the source SIM: 1 Btu = 0.293000 Wh, therefore 1 therm = 29.3 kWh. Monthly PS-E/PS-F values are printed as whole units; they are preserved exactly rather than adjusted to force agreement with separately rounded annual BEPU totals."
  },
